# What must NOT enter the build context.
#
# The image is built with `COPY packages ./packages` and `COPY services ./services`, and
# `npm run build` is `tsc -b` — which is INCREMENTAL. Without this file, a build run on a
# machine that has ever built locally copies that machine's dist/ and .tsbuildinfo into the
# context, and tsc can then decide there is nothing to recompile. The image ships whatever
# the developer's tree happened to hold, with no error and no way to tell from the outside.
#
# Everything below is either regenerated inside the build or has no business in an image.
node_modules
**/node_modules
dist
**/dist
*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.tsbuildinfo

.git
.gitignore
.github

# Working material, never part of a release.
runs
docs
# …except one file. architecture.html is SERVED by the gateway at /architecture, so it is part
# of the release even though everything else under docs/ is not. Excluding the directory and
# re-including the one file keeps a single copy in the repository — the alternative was a second
# copy under services/, which is how two versions of one document come to disagree.
!docs/architecture.html
.claude
testing
scripts

# Fixtures. `COPY catalog /catalog` takes the whole tree, and the `runs` line above matches
# the context ROOT only — so catalog/ops/ops-flow/tests (192 files, 2.3MB of requirements,
# steps and expectations) was shipping in every image. Nothing at runtime reads it: eval-judge
# and eval-grade read it from the repository, at test time. See docs/repository-architecture.md.
catalog/**/tests

# Local environment and build output.
deploy/.env
deploy/.env.*
dist/release
*.tgz
.DS_Store
